This tiny example finds a fictional library note by topic. It shows only retrieval; no AI answer is generated.

```javascript
const notes = [
  { topic: "hours", text: "The library closes at 5 pm." }
];
const match = notes.find(note => note.topic === "hours");
console.log(match.text);
```

It prints the note about closing time. A larger system must also handle finding no match.
